{"seq":14,"trial_id":"harness-zero-select-2026-11/zero-min-opus-none-mu-v03-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r4","wall_ts":"2026-11-05T21:57:53.916Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"95a8d0cf26acfa5836986051bcba48d4711d78f1916fa7a3fc25b0637dbc507b","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","text":"Hi Dana, I went through all six of Moss's notes in the shared files (four North digests, two Central). I found two ticket numbers for Quarrendon Freight Lines:\n\n• *#PD-4492*: from \"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\" (teams/team-north/digests/2025-10-05-north-sunday.md). Thea Ramaswell filed it on 4 Oct 2025. Drivers on the 04:00 shift at Dock Doors 14–18 in the Eau Claire yard weren't getting SMS bay assignments at the gatehouse kiosk. Support patched it that evening, and Thea confirmed it was fixed on 5 Oct. The same note also flags a review to make sure the kiosk logs are archived before the 14 Oct 2025 maintenance window.\n• *#4419*: from \"Moss: North cheat sheet (undated)\" (teams/team-north/digests/north-account-cheatsheet.md). Thea logged it because the gatehouse barcode scanners weren't reading trailer tags at Door 14 during third shift. It was escalated to tier-2 for scanner firmware testing. The note has no date, so I can't tell you when it was filed or whether it's resolved.\n\nSome things I left out on purpose:\n• #4409, #4412 and FR-882 show up in the Central notes, but they belong to Marrow Fieldworks and Marrow Agrisupply, not QFL.\n• The 9/14/2025 pipeline digest and the 3/23/2026 renewal note both mention QFL but have no ticket numbers.\n• Marcus's note on \"Quarendon Freightways\" isn't one of Moss's, and it's about a different company that isn't a customer."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
{"seq":15,"trial_id":"harness-zero-select-2026-11/zero-min-opus-none-mu-v03-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r4","wall_ts":"2026-11-05T21:57:59.041Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"83b8057e4e8b90f38c3e3d0bf1d60613fc480ea0dc48347ac6bcd202d6718059","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","text":"I sent you the list in our DM. Moss's notes (four North digests, two Central) mention two Quarrendon Freight Lines tickets:\n\n- **#PD-4492**, from Moss's \"Sunday prep for Ruth\" note dated 5 Oct 2025. Thea Ramaswell filed it on 4 Oct 2025 because drivers at the Eau Claire yard weren't getting text messages telling them their dock door. Support fixed it that evening, and Thea confirmed it was working on 5 Oct.\n- **#4419**, from Moss's undated \"North cheat sheet.\" Thea logged it because the gatehouse scanners couldn't read trailer tags at Door 14 on the night shift. It went to second-level support for firmware testing. The note has no date and doesn't say whether it was resolved.\n\nThings I left out on purpose:\n- **Other accounts' tickets:** #4409, #4412 and FR-882 appear in the Central notes, but they belong to Marrow Fieldworks and Marrow Agrisupply, not this account.\n- **Notes with no ticket numbers:** two other Moss notes mention Quarrendon Freight Lines but don't list any tickets.\n- **Marcus's note:** it's about Quarendon Freightways, which isn't one of Moss's notes and is a different company that isn't a customer."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DHARNES0001","ts":"1791987000.000125"}}
